WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.760
What's up with all the different lightsabers?

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:06.560
Luckily for you, we know which colors are
used by which kinds of folks, what they say

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.920
about the wielder's personality, and whether
or not a yellow lightsaber makes sense for

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.420
you.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.960
Here's the true meaning behind each lightsaber
color.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.020
The blue lightsaber is a classic for a reason.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.680
It's the iconic first lightsaber seen being
activated on screen in A New Hope, and since

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.310
both Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi had
one, it seems like the standard issue for

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.020
the Jedi Knights.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:31.440
Back in the day, a long time before "a long
time ago," it was established that a blue

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.600
lightsaber meant the user was a Jedi Guardian,
the samurai of the Jedi order.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.300
With their training focused on outer space
martial arts and lightsaber tomfoolery, Guardians

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.080
were warrior monks whose arrival heralded
a hasty round of limb removal.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.900
Especially if they had the higher ground.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.819
So what does this mean about the person behind
the lightsaber?

00:00:48.819 --> 00:00:52.199
Mainly that they could be a little more of
a soldier than your average Jedi, with the

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.140
blue saber functioning as their uniform.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.120
A green lightsaber was the calling card of
the Jedi Consulars, the thinking sentient's

00:00:59.120 --> 00:00:59.620
Jedi.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.140
Wielded in the films by folks like Qui-Gon
Jinn, the wise master Yoda, and an older and

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.540
more self-assured Luke Skywalker, green lightsaber
crystals seemed to indicate maturity and thoughtfulness.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.360
Or at least as thoughtful as you can be while
using them primarily to cut off people's hands,

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:13.860
anyway.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:18.140
Typically, Jedi Consulars were especially
Force sensitive, and they weren't generally

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.100
down for a fight in the same way that a Jedi
Guardian might be.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:26.100
They were diplomats, scholars, ambassadors,
and teachers, focusing on their studies and

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.950
the subtle art of space meditation, Wisdom
was their deal.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.400
As for the real-world reason, well, it's not
quite as philosophical.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:36.580
The first green lightsaber that fans saw in
Return of the Jedi was originally blue, but

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.259
the filmmakers realized that it was blending
in with the sky too much during the outdoor

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.260
action sequences.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.500
If you see a red lightsaber firing up in a
dark alley, a seedy bar, or God forbid, a

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.900
smoke-filled carbonite freezing chamber on
Bespin, then buddy, that's bad news.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.420
The red saber crystal is a hallmark of the
Sith, the nefarious bad guys of the Star Wars

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:55.920
canon.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.280
The distinctive red glow of a Sith lightsaber
comes from a particularly nasty construction

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.760
process that involves its wielder pouring
all of their negative emotions into a synthetic

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:05.260
crystal.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:09.459
Of course, a rough start in life doesn't always
mean that a crystal is doomed for good.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.660
Sometimes they get a shot at a re-branding
a little ways down the road.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.640
Purple, it's the universal sign of a hardcore
dude.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.620
For receipts, please see Prince, Thanos, Grimace,
and Mace Windu.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.200
And in the Star Wars universe?

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.599
A purple lightsaber represents a user's connection
to both the light and dark side of the Force,

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.090
wielded only by the most bold and daring Jedi.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.240
"You're impossibly outnumbered."

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.340
"I don't think so."

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.540
In the real world, which is occasionally even
more fun than the one with Jabba the Hutt

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.560
in it, purple lightsabers exist because Samuel
L. Jackson really wanted one.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.880
Since he was going to be in a scene with dozens
of other saber-wielding Jedi, he wanted to

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.120
be able to clock himself on the big screen,
and asked Lucas to give him a more distinctive

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:50.620
weapon.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.940
Bold and daring indeed.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.960
You may not have seen a yellow lightsaber
in the movies, but come on.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.440
This is Star Wars, and we all know how expanded
that universe can get.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:04.010
A yellow lightsaber was the preferred weapon
of the Jedi Sentinel, the pragmatic force-users

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.180
who skipped out on meditation and communing
with the universe in favor of developing more

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.240
practical skills.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.670
They were also frequently assigned as guards
of the Jedi Temple, sporting two-sided lightsaber

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.610
pikes with distinctive amber blades.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.040
For these guys, sabers were like a traffic
light: you see yellow, you better slow down.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:25.200
Even in the impossibly long list of characters
in the extended, pre-Disney Star Wars universe,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.700
there were only a few waving around orange
lightsabers.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.120
The most famous example was probably Yaddle,
the female member of Yoda's species who was

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:36.469
barely seen in The Phantom Menace and then
relegated to the pages of officially licensed

00:03:36.469 --> 00:03:37.460
books and comics.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:41.580
It's been speculated that orange sabers were
only owned by Jedi who swore not to use their

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.760
weapons unless absolutely necessary, and that
maybe that's why we never saw them in the

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:46.260
movies.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.220
Rare even by fictional weapon standards, the
white lightsaber borders on unique.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:55.780
In the current canon, these bright blades
belong to Ahsoka Tano, Anakin's old Padawan.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.220
It's a long story, but Ahsoka wound up being
one of the few characters to leave the Jedi

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.400
Order without immediately going to the dark
side.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:07.000
When she threw down with a Sith-affiliated
Jedi hunter, she nabbed the red crystals out

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.409
of his lightsaber and "cleansed" them with
the power of the Force, turning them a brilliant

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:13.120
but decidedly neutral white.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.740
For the Jedi who wants a weapon that goes
with everything, there's the black lightsaber.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:21.400
It's one of a kind, at least until the Star
Wars writers change their mind in a couple

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:21.900
of years.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.700
The "Darksaber" isn't just your everyday Jedi
weapon.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:28.660
It was the saber of one Tarre Vizsla, the
first Mandalorian Jedi.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.980
Mandalorians were pretty famous during the
Old Republic time period for their enthusiasm

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.560
about murdering Jedi, so a black lightsaber
was pretty fitting.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:40.980
The Darksaber wound up being handed down from
warrior to warrior throughout the millennia,

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:45.840
eventually being used in battles with all
of the usual suspects: Obi-Wan, Darth Maul,

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.140
and even Emperor Palpatine.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:51.380
According to the Mandalorians, the only way
to legitimately claim the blade for yourself

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:55.330
was to kill the person who had it before you,
making the weapon's history a long list of

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.380
bad times and badder people.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.860
These colors represent the lightsabers that
currently exist in the official Star Wars

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.800
continuity, but they don't even scratch the
surface of what fans have seen in the expanded

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.940
universe of Star Wars Legends books, games,
and comics.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.720
To the surprise of absolutely nobody, it seems
like just about every creative mind tasked

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:18.000
with telling a Star Wars story over the last
40-odd years has come up with their own distinctive

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.120
look for a lightsaber.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.300
Fans have listed nearly a hundred different
documented lightsaber colors, from the slightly

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.980
different to the downright bizarre.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:29.000
Lowbacca, one of the few Wookiee Jedi, had
a bronze-colored blade, for example.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.730
Really, just about any color you can imagine
(with the tragic exception of beige) is yours

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.040
for the claiming once you start down the Jedi
path.

